Description: Provides the R-facing interface for an open quantitative-genetic
    modelling system backed by the HSquared.jl Julia engine. Experimental
    0.9.0 experimental release (not production): the version tracks covered
    capability (public covered count is 7), not maturity; experimental label
    retained. CRAN submission is separately gated on one frozen artifact. Version 0.1 fits the univariate Gaussian
    animal model (y ~ fixed + animal(1 | id, pedigree = ped)) by restricted
    maximum likelihood and returns heritability, variance components, breeding
    values, and standard extractors. Default fitting requires a local Julia and
    HSquared.jl; use hs_control(engine = "validate") to preview the model
    contract without fitting. What you may report is listed on the package
    article 'Can I fit and report this?', not in validation_status(), which is
    a developer evidence table. Uncertainty intervals are experimental and not
    coverage-calibrated. Genomic GREML is covered at validation scale only on
    its explicit Julia target (`target = "genomic"`); the ordinary call remains
    the pedigree animal-model route. Experimental 0.9.0 retained; public
    covered count stays 7. Single-step, SNP-BLUP,
    repeatability, and two-effect animal models fit through opt-in engine paths
    (repeatability/two-effect covered where previously covered; SNP-BLUP
    remains experimental; single-step remains opt-in partial; Julia
    engine-covered is not R covered); multivariate cbind() animal models route
    on the default call and are covered at validation scale (t = 2 unstructured;
    k >= 3 and diagonal stay experimental); non-Gaussian
    (poisson(log)/binomial(logit)) models fit through an opt-in experimental
    conditional three-field engine path: logit observation-scale h2 is finite
    for Bernoulli and common-trial Binomial data, while varying trial counts
    return the explicit NaN sentinel because no scalar estimand is defined;
    no coverage-calibrated or covered claim is made; factor-analytic models
    remain planned.
